  "details": "Short version: there's an attached video\n\nLong version:\n\n- Publish any avatar\n\n- Increase the scale 6x (of the avatar, not of the armature)\n\n- Move the point of view to the correct position\n\n- Publish the avatar\n\n- A user use that avatar\n\n- Another user joins on a quest, and they don't have the avatar turned on\n\n- Quest user will see the fallback or the impostor\n\n- The fallback or impostor is 3x bigger than of the avatar size, with a very small hitbox in comparison\n\n I think it broke in a patch 2-3 months ago\n\nHere's a test avatar for proof (it's the most basic fbx. no phybones, fx layer, etc)\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_b16799d5-c5f4-4928-a8a8-72daff9e7e80\n\nAttached are \n\n- a pic of how it looks on PC (avatar is 10.74m). Everything is fine\n\n- a video of how it's broken on quest\n\nIt's kinda gamebreaking, because the avatar will have a small hitbox, username is hard to find, and it becomes really hard to block or to activate for quest users",
